# Dev reverse proxy. Plain HTTP on *.ventia.localhost — `.localhost` is a
# reserved special-use TLD (RFC 6761), so no publicly-trusted certificate
# exists or could exist for it, and none is needed locally.
http://api.ventia.localhost {
	reverse_proxy host.docker.internal:4000
}
http://admin.ventia.localhost {
	reverse_proxy host.docker.internal:3001
}
http://ventia.localhost, http://*.ventia.localhost {
	reverse_proxy host.docker.internal:3000
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Custom domains (SPEC.md §11 P6) — PRODUCTION shape, inert in dev.
#
# A merchant's own `tienda.example.com` cannot be enumerated ahead of time, so
# certificates are issued on demand: Caddy sees an unknown hostname in a TLS
# handshake and asks whether it may issue one.
#
# `ask` is the entire security boundary. Caddy issues only on a 2xx, and the
# endpoint below refuses unless the domain is registered, DNS-verified, owned
# by a LIVE tenant, and on a plan that includes custom domains — see
# services/api/src/tenants/custom-domains.service.ts, where each of those four
# conditions is separately mutation-tested.
#
# Without `ask`, anyone who points DNS at this platform makes Caddy request a
# certificate on our behalf. The damage is not that they get a certificate for
# their own domain — they could get that anywhere — it is that they exhaust
# the SHARED Let's Encrypt issuance rate limit and block renewal for every
# real tenant.
#
# The ask endpoint is reachable only from inside the compose network: it is
# mounted at `/internal/*` on the API, and no public site block below proxies
# that path. It is unauthenticated by necessity (Caddy calls it mid-handshake,
# before any session exists) and leaks nothing beyond whether a hostname is
# served here, which the handshake itself already reveals.
#
# Commented out in this dev Caddyfile because on-demand TLS needs a real
# public hostname and a reachable ACME endpoint, neither of which exists
# locally. Uncomment in the production Caddyfile.
#
# {
# 	on_demand_tls {
# 		ask http://api:4000/internal/tls-ask
# 		# Caddy's own second bound, independent of ours: even a bug that made
# 		# `ask` answer 200 for everything cannot burn the ACME budget faster
# 		# than this.
# 		interval 2m
# 		burst 5
# 	}
# }
#
# https:// {
# 	tls {
# 		on_demand
# 	}
# 	reverse_proxy storefront:3000
# }
